1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,573
The simplest crane in the world is

2
00:00:01,615 --> 00:00:03,483
a rope slung over a tree branch.

3
00:00:03,884 --> 00:00:04,528
It works,

4
00:00:04,718 --> 00:00:06,544
right up until the branch breaks.

5
00:00:06,839 --> 00:00:08,043
So you swap the tree for a

6
00:00:08,105 --> 00:00:08,940
steel tower,

7
00:00:09,077 --> 00:00:11,093
and bolt a long beam across the

8
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:11,631
top.

9
00:00:12,032 --> 00:00:13,446
That beam is called the jib.

10
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:15,631
But slide a load out along the

11
00:00:15,695 --> 00:00:16,138
jib,

12
00:00:16,486 --> 00:00:18,470
and the whole thing wants to topple.

13
00:00:19,104 --> 00:00:20,455
So you add a short arm facing

14
00:00:20,528 --> 00:00:21,088
backwards,

15
00:00:21,204 --> 00:00:22,998
and pile it with twenty tons of

16
00:00:23,062 --> 00:00:23,716
concrete.

17
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,215
That's the counterweight.

18
00:00:25,679 --> 00:00:26,524
Next problem:

19
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:28,096
your building is catching up with your

20
00:00:28,138 --> 00:00:28,624
crane.

21
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:30,418
So the crane climbs.

22
00:00:30,883 --> 00:00:32,814
Jacks raise everything above the tower,

23
00:00:32,973 --> 00:00:35,115
and a fresh six metre section slides

24
00:00:35,168 --> 00:00:35,906
into the gap.

25
00:00:36,371 --> 00:00:37,057
Keep going,

26
00:00:37,279 --> 00:00:38,640
and above eighty metres,

27
00:00:38,777 --> 00:00:40,593
the skinny tower flexes in the wind

28
00:00:40,677 --> 00:00:41,733
like a fishing rod.

29
00:00:42,282 --> 00:00:43,928
So you bring the crane indoors,

30
00:00:43,981 --> 00:00:46,018
into the shaft meant for the lifts.

31
00:00:46,419 --> 00:00:47,348
Every few floors,

32
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:49,480
it jacks itself up and braces against

33
00:00:49,523 --> 00:00:51,095
the concrete it just poured.

34
00:00:51,496 --> 00:00:53,205
Then the skyscraper is finished,

35
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:54,778
and you spot the flaw.

36
00:00:55,032 --> 00:00:56,266
The crane is on the roof,

37
00:00:56,404 --> 00:00:57,945
and nothing on the ground can reach

38
00:00:57,997 --> 00:00:58,272
it.

39
00:00:58,821 --> 00:01:00,415
So it hoists up a smaller crane,

40
00:01:00,552 --> 00:01:01,544
piece by piece.

41
00:01:01,945 --> 00:01:03,792
The small one dismantles the big one,

42
00:01:04,014 --> 00:01:05,428
and lowers it to the street.

43
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:08,151
Now the small crane is stranded.

44
00:01:08,615 --> 00:01:10,104
So an even smaller one takes that

45
00:01:10,145 --> 00:01:10,685
apart.

46
00:01:11,318 --> 00:01:12,415
And on it goes,

47
00:01:12,669 --> 00:01:14,474
until the last crane is so tiny,

48
00:01:14,537 --> 00:01:16,025
it goes home in the lift.

49
00:01:16,426 --> 00:01:17,165
Add a cab,

50
00:01:17,302 --> 00:01:17,840
a hook,

51
00:01:17,977 --> 00:01:19,951
and someone willing to climb up there

52
00:01:19,994 --> 00:01:20,743
at dawn.

53
00:01:21,292 --> 00:01:22,421
Congratulations.

54
00:01:22,885 --> 00:01:24,733
You've invented the tower crane.

